WEBVTT

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.740
You're the real Kiriyume?

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.150
Sorry, Hibiki.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:20.660
I was behind everything up until now.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:26.270
I ordered Yuzuha to act on my behalf.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.750
Yuzuha can't go against anything I tell her.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.210
Ever since she was born.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.300
I want you to forgive her.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:44.780
It was my fault for coming up with 
such childish, jealous, petty pranks.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.340
Yuzuha.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.610
Thanks for trying so hard 
to protect my mural.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.450
I'll be fine.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.580
As long as you're with me, I'll be fine.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.450
I'm sorry.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.070
I'm truly sorry.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.860
Hibiki.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.810
I enjoyed being connected to you.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.270
Goodbye.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.490
She's stuck on this island?

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.490
Yes.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:41.530
Until she finds a successor, 
Kiryu-sama is confined to this island.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.160
A successor?

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.380
If either she marries and has 
a child, or adopts a girl,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.500
and the girl turns five, 
she finally becomes free,

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.130
in exchange for her own child.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.340
Are you serious?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.610
Kiryu-sama is the dragon's priestess.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.450
She's a mitamashiro who's 
offered her own body.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:08.810
Therefore, aside from school, 
she spends her time alone in the shrine.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.980
It's strictly forbidden 
for her to show herself

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.940
or talk to people from outside the island.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.220
So I was really shocked 
when she broke the code

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:26.220
to show herself to Nukui-kun yesterday.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.440
I wanted her to experience the outside world,

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.970
even just a little, 
since she can't leave this island.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.090
Kiryu-sama has always loved drawing,

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:43.730
so I told her about an illustration uploader 
website, and she was really interested.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.970
She said she wanted to take part.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.350
I begged my parents to buy her a pen tablet.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:56.970
That's partly why I decided 
to pretend that I was Kiriyume.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.630
I see.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.070
Because that would have been safer.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.600
Yes.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.410
I thought some people on this 
island might not be as approving.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.440
I'm sorry.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.000
I'm full of lies.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.100
Not at all.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.890
I'm not angry anymore.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.250
I'll forgive you.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.380
Except...

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:23.260
I won't forgive you if you 
ever use centipedes again.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.010
I have a deathly fear of centipedes, too.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.770
I picked it up with a pair of tongs. 
I was nearly in tears when I threw it in.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.190
Then don't do it!

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:36.820
Kyo-nii.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.490
How is Kiriyume?

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.120
Aigae-san, have you talked 
to Kiriyume since?

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.660
I met with her before I came here.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.250
Did she say anything?

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.750
She said she's ending it.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:02.170
From now on, she's going to satisfy 
her duties as Kiryu's priestess.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:03.700
No...

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.040
Why?

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:05.930
Come on.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:07.610
Sakura?

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:10.030
What do you mean, "Why?"

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:13.430
You don't get to ask "why."

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.820
I think she's always wanted 
to be special to you.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:24.910
But with what happened, she's decided 
that things can't go back to normal.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:29.910
I think she's trying to forget everything 
so she doesn't let it drag on,

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.540
everything about being Kiriyume.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.260
No...

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.380
I believe that's what she is trying to do.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.130
Is that really true?

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.840
Is Kiriyume really okay with this?

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:01.270
With spending her life chained down 
at Kiryu Shrine against her will?

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.940
Why don't you ask her, then?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.610
If you don't know how someone 
feels, ask and find out.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.720
And tell them how you really feel.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:12.620
Right?

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:14.810
Yeah.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.960
That's Little Wing's policy.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.880
But it was decided only recently.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.690
Yeah.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.760
You're right.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.470
Nothing's going to change 
if we just sit here.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.670
Let's go to Kiriyume.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.070
Ku-chan's so fast.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:46.900
That girl should come with us if 
she's so worried about Kiriyume.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.650
She can't help it.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.370
She seems to have her own reasons.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:57.710
The Aigae family's always been tasked 
with taking care of Kiryu-sama.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:03.050
Therefore, I can't do any more to 
go against Kiryu-sama's wishes.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:04.960
I'm sorry.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.430
Guys.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.350
Hurry, hurry.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.150
Hurry up.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.900
Let's take a look around the building first.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.590
There might be an entrance somewhere.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.380
No good.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.760
It's locked.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.960
That's not surprising.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.220
It looks like there isn't an 
intercom or anything, either.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:48.010
Maybe we should have pleaded 
with Aigae-san to come with us.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.250
Having trouble, Kyo-san?

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:53.800
You are, aren't you?

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.020
Do you have a good idea, Jun?

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.770
Leave this to me.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.480
It's been a while since I've had 
a chance to make myself useful.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.650
<i>What is she doing?</i>

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.370
Jun's got superhuman ears.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:21.310
She wins right away when we play 
hide-and-seek and she's it.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:24.790
Kyo-san! Kyo-san!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.610
Did you find something?

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.970
I can hear a PC buzzing 
from beyond this wall.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.380
She might be on the other side.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.370
What do we do now, though?

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.540
What else would you do?

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:40.670
Just go for it!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.400
You did it, Kyo-san.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.940
Kiriyume, it's me.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.050
Hibiki?!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.450
Wh-Wh-Why?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.090
I want to talk to you.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.450
Please, come out.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.660
I won't!

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.900
Kiriyume...

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.710
Are you really happy with the way things are?

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.530
Do you really want to get rid of Kiriyume 
and pretend none of it ever happened?

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.290
Shut up!

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.630
Stop following me!

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:15.390
Kiriyume was just a way to waste time.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.270
It's over now!

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:26.340
She stopped answering after that.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:30.400
So we have no choice but 
to make a tactical retreat.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.230
But why are we here?

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.910
Kiriyume's mural is past here.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:48.900
It's almost gone.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.120
Too bad.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.420
I wanted to see it once more.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.880
So did I.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.930
That's why I wanted to come here.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:02.930
There was a drawing here that 
Kiriyume made based on my music.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:09.930
I think it was proof that 
Kiriyume and I had a connection.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.700
But now...

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:16.100
Don't be so down.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.160
The mural's gone,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.790
but I don't think it's as if the 
image is gone from Kiriyume's mind.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:27.330
<i>And as long as that still exists, 
so does my connection with her.</i>

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.910
You look like you have a plan.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.390
Yeah.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:40.430
There's only ever been one way to 
bring a reclusive god out of hiding.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.930
Where did I go wrong?

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:55.340
<i>There was no way I could ever 
get any closer to Hibiki.</i>

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:59.460
<i>Look what I did to the band 
girls, getting jealous.</i>

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:06.080
<i>To top it off, I tried to reach 
something I could never reach.</i>

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.500
<i>And I couldn't, and I got hurt.</i>

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:13.190
<i>I'm such an idiot.</i>

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.470
A collaboration?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.570
Yes.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.670
Between Lien de Famille 
and the island drummers.

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:28.550
Could we play a song together?

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:31.270
Yes, that sounds delightful.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.300
But what song?

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:36.230
Do you have an idea, Manager?

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.490
Yes, I do.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.740
Thank goodness.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.790
So we can collaborate 
with the island drummers.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.080
I can't wait.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.310
I feel bad, though, in a way.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:57.090
What do you think the islanders will say 
if they find out what we're trying to do?

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:01.020
What we're trying to do is to 
collaborate with the island drummers.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.640
We haven't asked for any more than that.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.390
That's surprisingly proactive, 
coming from you.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.300
Yeah.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.640
I decided I'm going to stop hesitating.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.550
What do you think?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.390
I have an old tablet that I used to use.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.650
I think I can find the other equipment, too.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:26.910
But as a member of the Aigae family, 
I can't betray Kiryu-sama any more.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.410
I don't know if we'll 
actually end up using it.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:33.710
Would it be too much to 
ask just to prepare it?

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:40.260
Hey, do you really think things 
are okay the way they are?

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.580
Kiriyume—your beloved friend—

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.970
is about to give up on a lot of 
things for the sake of tradition.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:49.990
Are you okay with that?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.980
It hurts when you say it like that.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:58.130
<i>Sorry, Aigae-san, for putting it like that.</i>

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.290
If you'll promise...

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:07.120
you won't tell Kiryu-sama 
anything ahead of time.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.830
You'll only do what Kiryu-sama herself wants.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.350
If you can promise that...

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.100
All right.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:15.210
I'll promise.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.090
<b>First Soryu Island Revitalization</b>

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.230
I'm getting nervous.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.650
Do you need to pee again, Jun-tan?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.360
What?

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:40.480
We're up.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:48.700
Um...

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.470
Nice to meet you.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:57.350
We're Lien de Famille.

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.590
We came here on a boat.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.420
How else would you have got here?

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:04.890
Um...

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.340
Uh...

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.130
Thank you for waiting.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:49.140
Now that we're ready, we'll play a 
special song just for this event.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:14:08.030
<i>Hear the soul</i>

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:19.930
<i>Hear the glimmering</i>

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:34.060
<i>Hear the soul</i>

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:46.310
<i>Hear the glimmering</i>

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:59.420
<i>I wanted to embrace you 
like a warm bowl of soup</i>

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:06.090
<i>It turned out, you felt the same way</i>

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:11.590
<i>I was surprised, but even more, I was happy</i>

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:18.100
<i>You can't help but smile</i>

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:25.820
<i>The treasure I'd been looking 
for was right here all along</i>

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:32.570
<i>My love for you will never die, 
whether you cry or become stubborn</i>

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:46.450
<i>Listen carefully, and you'll hear</i>

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.630
<i>You see, even today</i>

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:54.270
<i>The invisible treasure</i>

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.890
That's enough!

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:09.180
K-Kiryu-sama.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.150
Why?

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:20.040
How dare you all leave me 
out to enjoy yourselves?!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.040
You sheeple!

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.030
Kiriyume.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:31.550
We finally get to meet again.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:33.930
You got me.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.180
I snapped and stormed out.

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.140
And this is exactly what you wanted?

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.190
Yeah.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.890
I really wanted to see you again.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:47.410
There's something I want 
to talk to you about.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:50.280
You may not.

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:55.300
Kiryu-sama must not speak 
so closely with an outsider.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.630
Please return to the shrine.

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:00.980
Otherwise the island will be met by disaster.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:03.540
Wait, please.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.020
Aigae-san.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:10.750
Please, give her freedom, just for now.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.460
Yuzuha...

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.690
What do you think you're doing, Yuzu-chan?

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:18.430
Do you really think an Aigae has 
the right to say such a thing?

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.660
Yuzu-chan doesn't have the right, huh?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.020
Then what about me?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.010
Sayuri-san, what do you mean by that?

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:30.820
What else could I mean?

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:33.500
I'm the previous Kiryu priestess.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:38.490
Would you brush me off for asking 
for my own daughter's happiness?

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.990
Mom...

00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:45.500
What?

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:51.100
So what do you want to talk to me about?

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:55.470
Are you really okay with this?

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:57.880
I'm not.

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:00.580
I finally got to connect with you.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.560
I don't want it to end now.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.890
But I'm the Kiryu priestess.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:07.440
That doesn't matter.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:12.020
I'm not from this island, so I don't 
know much about its traditions.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:16.190
So this might be a blasphemous 
thing to ask for.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:19.970
But I want to remain connected with you.

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:22.530
Hibiki....

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:23.650
Please.

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:26.250
I want you to continue to color my music.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.330
That mural...

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:32.170
The world you created from my music.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.420
I want you to bring it back.

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:40.030
Okay.

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:43.930
Looks like you're done talking.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.020
Can you check on the PC stuff?

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.120
Everything else is set.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.050
Yeah.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.210
I'll be right there.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:04.270
Didn't you honestly think something was off 
when you first heard about Kiryu Shrine?

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:06.880
Well, sure, a little.

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:09.100
You don't have to be so polite.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.670
But that was normal on this island.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.270
It was always that way.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:17.470
It was normal.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:21.410
So I wanted to end it.

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:25.180
Ever since I was Kiryu's priestess.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:29.770
So then the island revitalization event...

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.770
<b>First Soryu Island Revitalization</b>

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.460
Exactly.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:35.070
I thought maybe if we brought some 
people from outside to interact with,

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:39.220
the sentiments on the island 
might change just a little.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.030
<b>Island Revitalization!</b>

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.030
Tourist attractions

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.030
Island's popularity

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:40.030
Local specialties exhibit

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:44.660
And that maybe we might decide 
to end this tradition someday.

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:47.270
You think it's pretty roundabout, don't you?

00:19:48.010 --> 00:19:52.420
I've thought of more extreme 
measures, but I couldn't do it.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:59.630
I worried that I might be too forceful 
and cause friction among the islanders.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:06.780
She's going to be living on this island, 
at least until she's independent.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:12.590
Sorry, I never thought about that.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:16.770
I was the one who hadn't thought it through.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:21.530
With the way I was doing 
things, even if it worked,

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.220
I might have taken it too slowly to save her.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.550
Thank you for being connected with her.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:31.910
Please take care of her going forward, too.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.170
Okay.

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.010
Come back again.

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:37.750
Thank you very much.

00:22:38.100 --> 00:22:40.160
I promise we'll be back.

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:42.250
Goodbye.

00:22:45.770 --> 00:22:49.260
Kiriyume-san didn't come to say bye.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:52.860
She vanished right after the concert.

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:56.150
A message.

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:58.250
It's from Kiriyume.

00:22:58.230 --> 00:23:00.230
Sender: Kiriyume
Later.

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:02.560
She's so cold.

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:04.570
There's an attachment.

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:07.070
Isn't this...

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:09.430
It's the one she drew for the concert.

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:12.750
Except she's smiling.

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:24.960
<b>The Grade School Kids Might've
Not Been Able to Save the Drowning God
if They Hadn't Gotten There in Time</b>

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:26.860
What?!

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>10: Totally a Date</b>

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:28.880
Why am I repenting?

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:31.450
I'll have you know I'm a god.

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:33.620
People worship me.

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:36.870
People should be repenting to <i>me</i>.

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:38.160
Trial by water!

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:39.930
But I said I'm a god!
